KG42.register("rules-786bef38fce402435d40aea1",{"id":"37-dsm_auction_incentives::v141-c-R005","paper":"37-dsm_auction_incentives","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Energy-trade execution","process_stage":"activation","market_meaning":"The provider completes the social-welfare consumption-allocation optimization, reduced to cost minimization under fixed daily consumption totals, before users begin the corresponding energy-consumption cycle. Scope: Enhanced AGV DSM procedure: consumption-allocation optimization followed by the corresponding consumption cycle. Condition: Each user's declared daily consumption total is held fixed; only its hourly consumption distribution is optimized. Users' payment obligations are set and announced before the corresponding actual energy consumption begins. Scope: Enhanced AGV DSM procedure: setting and announcing payment obligations for the next consumption cycle.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function execution.energy_trade under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.social_welfare","execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e001","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e011"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E002","source":"settlement.payment","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g02-e012"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Enhanced AGV DSM procedure: consumption-allocation optimization followed by the corresponding consumption cycle. | Enhanced AGV DSM procedure: setting and announcing payment obligations for the next consumption cycle.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e001","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g02-e012"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R005-x_i","symbol":"\\mathbf{x}_i","meaning":"User i's hourly power-consumption allocation vector; component x_i^s is user i's power consumption in time slot s. It is selected by the cost-minimization allocation rule (19).","kind":"design_selection","domain":"\\mathcal{X}_i (user i's feasible energy consumption set)","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e001","v141-b-g02-e007"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta_hat","symbol":"\\hat{\\theta}","meaning":"Vector/profile of users' declared demand information supplied to the allocation rule x(\\hat{\\theta}) in source equation (19).","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\hat{\\theta}"},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-C_s","symbol":"C_s","meaning":"Cost of providing energy in time slot s as a function of aggregate consumption in that slot, as used in source equation (19) and defined in source equation (2).","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"C_s(\\cdot)"},"unit":null,"indices":["s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e001","v141-b-g02-e007"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The provider completes the social-welfare consumption-allocation optimization, reduced to cost minimization under fixed daily consumption totals, before users begin the corresponding energy-consumption cycle. Scope: Enhanced AGV DSM procedure: consumption-allocation optimization followed by the corresponding consumption cycle. Condition: Each user's declared daily consumption total is held fixed; only its hourly consumption distribution is optimized.","expression":"\\mathbf{x}(\\hat{\\theta}) = \\arg\\min_{\\mathbf{x}_i \\in \\mathcal{X}_i,\\, i\\in\\mathcal{N}} \\sum_{s\\in\\mathcal{S}} C_s\\left(\\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_i^s\\right) \\quad \\text{(source eq. (19))}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x_i"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-theta_hat","v141-c-R005-C_s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e001","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e011"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Users' payment obligations are set and announced before the corresponding actual energy consumption begins. Scope: Enhanced AGV DSM procedure: setting and announcing payment obligations for the next consumption cycle.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g02-e012"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e001","location":{"location_id":"src-d83df5b2d1-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Problem Formulation and Mechanism Solution / B. Problem Formulation","anchor_text":"MA et al.: INCENTIVE MECHANISM FOR DEMAND SIDE MANAGEMENT IN SMART GR B. Problem Formulation co tru ","equation_id":"(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Since we apply the utility function to represent users’ benefits through electricity consumption, we can use the sum of all users’ utility functions to indicate the social benefit of electricity consumption. Hence, we consider a social objective, which is to maximize the social benefit while minimizing the cost of providing that amount of electricity. This can be represented by the following problem: \\[ \\max_{\\mathbf{x}_i \\in \\mathcal{X}_i, i\\in\\mathcal{N}} \\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{N}} U_i\\left(\\sum_{s\\in\\mathcal{S}} x_i^s\\right) - \\sum_{s\\in\\mathcal{S}} C_s\\left(\\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_i^s\\right), \\tag{15} \\] where \\mathbf{x}_i is user i’s power consumption vector, U_i(\\cdot) is as in (14), and C_s(\\cdot) is as in (2). The proposed energy consumption schedule is the solution of (15). Meanwhile, problem (15) is a concave maximization, which can be solved by convex programming such as the interior point method (IPM) [29]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-d83df5b2d1-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Problem Formulation and Mechanism Solution / C. Proposed Mechanism","anchor_text":". 2) Social Objective: We deﬁne the social objective in the as form of 6) where is the set of all us","equation_id":"(18)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"3) Optimal Consumption Vector: The optimal consumptive vector is set by the allocation rule \\mathbf{x}(\\hat{\\theta}) defined as follows. For a given vector of the declared demand information \\hat{\\theta} = \\{\\hat{\\theta}_1,\\ldots,\\hat{\\theta}_N\\}, the AGV mechanism chooses the consumption allocation \\mathbf{x}(\\hat{\\theta}) as the optimal solution to (15), and it calculates the optimal consumption vectors as \\[ \\mathbf{x}(\\hat{\\theta}) = \\arg\\max_{\\mathbf{x}_i \\in \\mathcal{X}_i, i\\in\\mathcal{N}} \\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{N}} U_i\\left(\\sum_{s\\in\\mathcal{S}} x_i^s\\right) - \\sum_{s\\in\\mathcal{S}} C_s\\left(\\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_i^s\\right). \\tag{18} \\]"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-d83df5b2d1-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Problem Formulation and Mechanism Solution / C. Proposed Mechanism","anchor_text":"(18) 7) We suppose that the energy provider does not change the de- clared amount of every user’s da","equation_id":"(19), (20)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We suppose that the energy provider does not change the declared amount of every user’s daily power consumption. We only optimize users’ hourly consumptive distribution. Thus, the problem in (18) can be reduced to \\[ \\mathbf{x}(\\hat{\\theta}) = \\arg\\min_{\\mathbf{x}_i \\in \\mathcal{X}_i, i\\in\\mathcal{N}} \\sum_{s\\in\\mathcal{S}} C_s\\left(\\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_i^s\\right). \\tag{19} \\]"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e011","location":{"location_id":"src-d83df5b2d1-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Problem Formulation and Mechanism Solution / C. Proposed Mechanism","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 5, NO. 3, MAY 2014 he TABLE I ch PRICING METHOD USING THE ENHA","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table I","image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"TABLE I PRICING METHOD USING THE ENHANCED AGV MECHANISM 1. Registered users submit the energy demand for the next consumption cycle. * Each user selects the types of appliances and decides each type’s energy demand. The smart meter computes \\hat{x}_i and \\hat{\\psi}_i. * \\hat{\\theta}_i = \\{\\mathbf{B}_i, \\mathbf{b}_i, \\mathbf{x}_i\\}, \\psi_i and user’s consumption record will be submitted to the energy provider. 2. The energy provider optimizes users’ consumption allocations and set the payments. * Optimize users’ consumption allocations based on the submitted information by solving (19). * Compute the values of users’ payments using (20) and (23). * Announce the recommended consumption allocations and payments to users. 3. The users start the new consumption cycle, and the smart meters record users’ consumption information. Return to 1."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-d83df5b2d1-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Problem Formulation and Mechanism Solution / C. Proposed Mechanism","anchor_text":"Our pricing method is summarized in Table I. Proposition 1: By using the enhanced AGV mechanism, use","equation_id":"(22), (23)","figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table I","image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Proposition 1: By using the enhanced AGV mechanism, user i can gain its largest payoff when it reports its true private information to the provider. Proof: The real payoff of user i can be written as \\[ P_i(\\mathbf{x}_i(\\theta)) = P_i^{norm}(\\mathbf{x}_i(\\theta)) - ct_i(\\theta_{-i}, \\hat{\\theta}_{-i}), \\] where P_i^{norm} is the real payoff (payoff after consumption) of user i using (22) and ct_i(\\theta_{-i}, \\hat{\\theta}_{-i}) is the extra part in (23). So \\[ P_i(\\mathbf{x}_i(\\theta)) = U_i\\left(\\sum_{s\\in\\mathcal{S}} x_i^s\\right) - t_i(\\theta) - ct_i(\\theta_{-i}, \\hat{\\theta}_{-i}), \\] where t_i(\\theta) is set before consumption. Before consumption, it is proved in [3] that the best strategy for user to declare its plan is to declare \\theta = \\hat{\\theta}. However, the user can draw back and consume more to get better payoff since there is no punishment."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-settlement","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e011","quote":"2. The energy provider optimizes users’ consumption allocations and set the payments. * Optimize users’ consumption allocations based on the submitted information by solving (19). * Compute the values of users’ payments using (20) and (23). * Announce the recommended consumption allocations and payments to users. 3. The users start the new consumption cycle, and the smart meters record users’ consumption information."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e006","quote":"the AGV mechanism chooses the consumption allocation \\mathbf{x}(\\hat{\\theta}) as the optimal solution to (15)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e001","quote":"Hence, we consider a social objective, which is to maximize the social benefit while minimizing the cost of providing that amount of electricity."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e007","quote":"We suppose that the energy provider does not change the declared amount of every user’s daily power consumption. We only optimize users’ hourly consumptive distribution."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e012","quote":"where t_i(\\theta) is set before consumption."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e011","quote":"Announce the recommended consumption allocations and payments to users. 3. The users start the new consumption cycle, and the smart meters record users’ consumption information."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"5d0dad30cbde499ba404aaf08b6b3d168094dfdb065e54716735400b5cbd7c19","applicability":"formalized","reason":"C001's allocation component is formalized from source equation (19): under fixed declared daily totals, the reduced clearing allocation is the cost-minimizing consumption vector. The temporal precedence is not encoded by a new time symbol; it remains represented by frozen edge E001. C002 remains non-formalized because the source states payment timing only procedurally and the payment formula belongs to settlement rule R006, not this rule. All support is from supplied, still-unreviewed candidate B evidence.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-x_i","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E001"],"rationale":"x_i is the argmin variable in source equation (19), selected at clearing.social_welfare and then carried into execution.energy_trade as the announced consumption allocation; frozen edge E001 encodes the clearing-before-execution relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-theta_hat","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Declared demand information is the input profile to x(\\hat{\\theta}) in equation (19) at clearing.social_welfare. The frozen R005 graph has no bidding.demand node or incoming edge, so none is asserted."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C_s","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C_s is the source cost function in the objective of equation (19), evaluated at aggregate time-slot consumption at clearing.social_welfare."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E001"],"rationale":"C001 requires the clearing allocation from equation (19) to be completed before execution. The expression formalizes the allocation rule; the ordering component is represented by frozen edge E001 rather than by an invented temporal symbol."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E002"],"rationale":"C002 is the frozen precedence relation E002: payment obligations are set and announced at settlement.payment before actual consumption at execution.energy_trade. No payment formula is introduced because that mathematics is owned by settlement rule R006."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
